<p>At the core of politics is a “team”. It is a fulfilment of the basic desire to belong. When you are red or blue, you are part of a team, and that team can do no wrong. Futhermore, those that are on the other team are the “enemy”.</p>
<p>It’s enough to have these viewpoints at a sports match. Where you can simply walk out of the arena and be friends with the guy who cheered for the other team.</p>
